		{"id":"045be703ee587ddf","type":"text","text":"Meta Inference (Ontology)\n\n- **Batch** \n\t- Business entity*****\n\t\t- Table Level\n\t\t\t- Business entity\n\t\t\t\t- Business Ontology\n\t\t\t- Self Join ( RAG)\n\t\t\t\t- Extra explict domain/Relationship context\n\t\t\t- Foreign Keys\n\t\t\t\t- Actual Relationship/Ontology\n\t\t\t- Strong FP&A DQ Rules\n\t\t\t\t-Possible ones\n\t\t- Embeddings\n\t\t\t- Business Ontology\n\t\t\t- Actual Context\n\t\t\t\t- \n\n\t- Column\n\t\t- Business definction\n\t\t\t- Business context of FP&A and possible relationships - Possible\n\t\t\t- Table Level \n\t\t\t- Business level ontology  - Actuals\n\t\t- Cross Reference\n\t\t- \n\t- Edges\n","x":1638,"y":578,"width":762,"height":742,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"791507fa61af2437","x":1360,"y":1760,"width":1200,"height":460,"color":"5","type":"text","text":"- DQ Inference \n\t- 50 Predined rules\n\t\t- Break the predifned rules into RAG queries ( Single atomic fields)\n\t\t\t- Build RAG queries with FP&A ontology context \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t- Column_metadata\n\t\t\t\t- Business Ontology at column level \n\t\t\t\t\t- Table Context - ?\n\t\t\t\t- Possible DQ rules context ( halunicate)\n\n\"The account_id column is a string data type with a maximum length of 10 characters, representing unique identifiers for accounts. It is a primary key in the chart_of_accounts table, ensuring each account can be distinctly referenced. This column is essential for operational and analytical use cases, such as financial reporting and account management. The data is sourced from the financial system and is updated regularly to reflect new accounts. Quality rules dictate that this field must be unique and non-nullable. Expected formats include numeric strings, and known value patterns are typically sequential or hierarchical. This column is used in filters, joins, and aggregations for reporting and compliance purposes. There are no regulatory or privacy considerations for this field.\",\n\nSQL query as a output\n\n\n"},
		{"id":"bfc48a8a249f11e5","x":2670,"y":1446,"width":420,"height":294,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"- Omega Inferences\n- Omega Verification determiniscitlaly\n\t\t- FK\n- Human in the Loop \n\t- PK\n\t- FK\n\t- Cross Reference \n- Conversation Context \n\t- BAD Context ?"},
